PROTECTED (AEvo)

These files define what this block PROMISES. An agent improving this block may TIGHTEN them
but may not LOOSEN them without human approval.

  port.ts    — the boundary contract. May add a method, narrow a type, add a guarantee.
               May NOT remove a method, widen a return, or drop a guarantee (including the
               injectable executor seam, the surfaced-exit-code contract, path validation,
               and the no-secret-leak promise).
  gates.ts   — the protected evaluator. May ADD a gate, RAISE a threshold, ADD a requirement.
               May NOT remove a gate, lower a threshold, or drop a requirement.

Tightening is automatic. Loosening requires the human. The structural half of this is
enforced by gates.assertNoLoosening(committed, proposed); the semantic half (a human reading
a threshold change) is the human's job.

Everything else in this block (adapters/*, demo.ts, insights.md) is freely editable.
